Z||000000||Adrift||11-07-2001||01:36 PM||||I brought my battery in and got it charged fully - Now I get a response when I turn the key! When I turn the key once the "Engine service" light flicks once and then stays on. When I then turn the key again (To start the engine, I'm also holding down the clutch at this point) I hear the sound of something "returning to its orignal position" (That's the best I can describe it, almost as if something is whipping back into place) and the whole car goes dead. The car stays dead (no lights, no response, NOTHING) for the next 10-20 minutes, then out of the blue it starts up again (NOt the engine, just the electrical system, as described in the begining) and the whole process repeates itself. Any Ideas?||||reg||8
Z||000001||SKIDMARK||11-07-2001||01:42 PM||||Sounds to me like maybe a bad starter solenoid or the electrical cable connection at the solenoid or battery. Make sure all the battery and cable connections are clean and free of corrosion. Check the other end of the cables too....at the starter and the ground on the engine block. If anything looks corroded, repair or replace it.<P>------------------<BR>White '85 4cyl coupe<BR>Black '86 v-6 SE<BR>'81 CB900F Super Sport||||reg||1
Z||000002||Adrift||11-07-2001||02:16 PM||||Looks like a lot of the connections are a little rusty, I'll have to get those cleaned up<BR>Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
